cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Goudreau
    given-names: Antoine
title: "The Musical Neuron (le neurone musical): a Max/MSP tool for co-comprovisation"
type: software
keywords:
  - Max/MSP
  - co-comprovisation
  - computer-assisted composition
  - improvisation
  - melodic analysis
  - Bach
  - Cage
  - Dada
  - Deleuze
repository-code: "https://github.com/epphone/musical-neuron"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  The Musical Neuron transcribes an improvised monodic phrase of one breath-length,
  analyzes it, reduces it to a spatial-notation line (held notes and glissandi),
  and feeds it back to the performer, who re-improvises over each iteration of
  the line. The analysis pipeline (rhythmic-distribution markers, slicing into
  basic melodic units, median-based merging and splitting, melodic reduction
  against idealized contour profiles) is described in the repository documentation;
  its conceptual foundations are developed in the included essay (in French).
